Here is an analysis of the cellular composition of the specified multicellular structures within the kidney, detailing the enriched and sparse cell types for each.

Proximial tubules:
Enriched: Tubular cells (CD183++/CD227-)
Sparse: Distal tubular cells (CD227+), Smooth muscle cells (aSMA+)

Distal tubules:
Enriched: Distal tubular cells (CD227+)
Sparse: Tubular cells (CD183++/CD227-)

Glomeruli:
Enriched: Endothelial cells (CD31+/CD196+), Nestin+ cells (nestin+)
Sparse: Tubular cells (CD183++/CD227-), Distal tubular cells (CD227+)

Blood vessel:
Enriched: Smooth muscle cells (aSMA+)
Sparse: Tubular cells (CD183++/CD227-), Distal tubular cells (CD227+)

Interstitium:
Enriched: Endothelial cells (CD31+/CD196+), Low expressing cells, Immune cells (CD45+/CD68+/CD11b+)
Sparse: Tubular cells (CD183++/CD227-), Distal tubular cells (CD227+)